WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
There's this war that most people haven't&nbsp;
heard about. It's the war in Bosnia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.340
and it happened in like the early ‘90s. Big&nbsp;
thing that you learn when you study this war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.980
is that there was a full blown genocide taking&nbsp;
place and the international community could have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.720
stopped it. The U.N. was actually there trying&nbsp;
to kind of stop it, but they didn't. It's easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.700
to think that the U.N. is like this big like&nbsp;
global policeman, or like that it has some power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.440
but the U.N. is just composed of a bunch of&nbsp;
countries. U.N. soldiers are just soldiers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.060
from other countries that the countries sent&nbsp;
to be a part of the U.N. In the early ’90s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.440
there weren't a lot of countries who wanted to&nbsp;
get involved in a conflict in Bosnia. So because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.760
of this, the U.N. presence in Bosnia didn't&nbsp;
really affect much. It didn't stop terrible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.260
things from happening. It's one of several&nbsp;
instances in the 1990s that the U.N. could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.280
have stepped in and stop horrible things from&nbsp;
happening, but didn't. And we learned big lessons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.720
from that. We made a whole video about this,&nbsp;
actually, and mapped the whole thing. And it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:56.280
just pretty wild to see how the world can fail&nbsp;
to stop something so horrible from happening.

